            <ArticleTitle>Prognostic value of exercise stress myocardial perfusion imaging in patients with permanent pacemakers.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>811-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>One hundred eight patients with single- or dual-chamber pacemakers underwent exercise myocardial perfusion imaging with thallium-201 or technetium-99m sestamibi. A high-risk scan (a large fixed defect, a large reversible defect, or evidence of cardiomyopathy) identified patients at high risk for cardiac death on both a univariate and multivariate basis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
